1
00:00:00,245 --> 00:00:02,920
AI assistants have started shopping for people.

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:04,795
But PayPal's agent checkout is built

3
00:00:04,795 --> 00:00:06,808
for merchants with a website store.

4
00:00:06,808 --> 00:00:08,533
Rosa bakes from her kitchen.

5
00:00:08,533 --> 00:00:11,283
She has no website, just this sheet of paper.

6
00:00:11,283 --> 00:00:14,845
One home baker in Virginia took orders in texts and DMs,

7
00:00:14,845 --> 00:00:16,732
then tracked them on a spreadsheet.

8
00:00:16,732 --> 00:00:20,583
In a 2016 Census survey, nearly half of US food

9
00:00:20,583 --> 00:00:23,333
and lodging employer firms had no website.

10
00:00:23,333 --> 00:00:26,750
An assistant can't order from a sheet of paper.

11
00:00:27,678 --> 00:00:29,715
Shelfie starts with one photo.

12
00:00:29,715 --> 00:00:33,133
Rosa snaps her price list, and Claude reads it.

13
00:00:34,945 --> 00:00:37,470
Shelfie only asks about what it isn't sure of,

14
00:00:37,470 --> 00:00:40,520
like a price written as two for seven dollars.

15
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:42,520
Rosa adds her PayPal email,

16
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:44,632
so buyers pay her directly.

17
00:00:44,632 --> 00:00:47,958
Every item becomes a product in PayPal's catalog.

18
00:00:47,958 --> 00:00:50,333
In our tests, photo to live shop took

19
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:53,300
8 to 14 seconds of machine time.

20
00:00:54,587 --> 00:00:56,200
Items she hasn't photographed show

21
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:59,000
an example photo, labelled as one.

22
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,725
Then one more photo, of her display case:

23
00:01:01,725 --> 00:01:05,142
Claude finds each item in it, and crops her own.

24
00:01:06,403 --> 00:01:08,128
The shop gets an agent door,

25
00:01:08,128 --> 00:01:09,928
and a card for the counter.

26
00:01:09,928 --> 00:01:11,253
Regulars scan it,

27
00:01:11,253 --> 00:01:14,383
or give the shop's link to their own assistant.

28
00:01:14,662 --> 00:01:16,062
This is Claude Code,

29
00:01:16,062 --> 00:01:18,624
given nothing but the shop's web address.

30
00:01:18,624 --> 00:01:21,037
The shop tells it where the agent door is.

31
00:01:21,037 --> 00:01:23,362
It reads the menu, places the order,

32
00:01:23,362 --> 00:01:26,467
and hands back a PayPal approval link.

33
00:01:29,287 --> 00:01:30,912
Buyers without an assistant get

34
00:01:30,912 --> 00:01:32,775
one right on the shop page.

35
00:01:32,775 --> 00:01:34,962
This buyer wants almond croissants,

36
00:01:34,962 --> 00:01:37,024
and mentions a nut allergy.

37
00:01:37,024 --> 00:01:39,812
The assistant warns that they contain nuts.

38
00:01:39,812 --> 00:01:43,342
The buyer confirms, and it places the order.

39
00:01:46,128 --> 00:01:48,978
The buyer logs in to PayPal and approves.

40
00:01:48,978 --> 00:01:51,291
Shelfie captures the payment, and the money

41
00:01:51,291 --> 00:01:55,383
lands in Rosa's own PayPal account, not ours.

42
00:01:57,662 --> 00:01:59,712
And agents can't set prices.

43
00:01:59,712 --> 00:02:02,492
The server checks that, not the model.

44
00:02:03,845 --> 00:02:06,908
Rosa's dashboard shows the order as paid.

45
00:02:06,908 --> 00:02:09,332
A Claude agent reads PayPal's record

46
00:02:09,332 --> 00:02:11,895
of the order through the PayPal Agent Toolkit,

47
00:02:11,895 --> 00:02:13,420
and writes her a brief.

48
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:15,220
It catches the nut allergy,

49
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:18,325
so she can check with the buyer before shipping.

50
00:02:19,653 --> 00:02:20,903
She adds tracking,

51
00:02:20,903 --> 00:02:23,708
and the buyer's assistant reads it back.

52
00:02:26,045 --> 00:02:28,233
Shelfie turns a photo of a price list into

53
00:02:28,233 --> 00:02:31,358
prepaid orders, from any AI assistant,

54
00:02:31,358 --> 00:02:34,145
paid into the seller's own PayPal account.

55
00:02:34,145 --> 00:02:35,333
It's for the sellers agent

56
00:02:35,333 --> 00:02:37,158
commerce hasn't reached yet.

57
00:02:37,158 --> 00:02:40,675
For Rosa, a sheet of paper is now enough.
